Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||04-18-2001||12:15 AM||||i was driving around to go do some onsite networking in the big compusa van and stopped at a light looking at my directions, when i hear a familiar sound, rump rump rump rump - i know that sound! haven't heard it in months! (busted fiero) i look up - white formula, beautiful! wasn't in the best condition, but it was a fiero, so it was beautiful! i missed my turn because i was so into hearing it run... it was cool!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460757&p=25516673&Sequence=0&res=high"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||04-18-2001||02:18 AM||||Oddly enough I was in Oceanside today...<P>But I wasn't in a Fiero, I was in a 2001 VW Beetle Turbo with Loren Freese (It was his but he also drives a Mera) doing a dry run of giant road trip that Fieros West is doing next month (the road trip concludes in Oceanside). I wanted to see what a Bug could do and it was roomy enough for all of the maps we had to open up and notes we were taking. We learned a lot (including a part of a road that was closed off) but will have to do another dry run ideally before the end of the month. We saw a couple of Fieros but no white Formulas. Hopefully, on May 12 you might hear several Fieros rumbling into town!<P>Gorgeous day for a drive too!||||reg||6
